    <h2>Synopsis & Production Background</h2>
    <p>
        Set in a rain-soaked megalopolis in the year 2084, <em>"Echoes of Tomorrow"</em> traces the story of an acoustic archaeologist who reconstructs erased memories from electromagnetic field resonance left behind in decommissioned skyscrapers.
    </p>

    <p>
        Captured natively on 70mm IMAX cameras with custom anamorphic lenses, director Denis Moreau prioritizes practical lighting, authentic miniature sets, and brutalist architecture over green screens.
    </p>

    <blockquote>
        "Our goal with the teaser and the score was to pull audiences into a tactile, living world where the sound design is indistinguishable from the musical score."
        <br><br><strong>— Denis Moreau, Director</strong>
    </blockquote>

    <h2>The Original Soundtrack Score</h2>
    <p>
        Composer Hansel Vance recorded the 18-piece string ensemble at Abbey Road Studio Two, layering cello glissandos over customized Buchla and Moog modular synthesizer systems. The result is a brooding, propulsive soundscape that has already generated intense social media conversation ahead of the film's premiere at the Venice Film Festival.
    </p>
